Package: Decant
Title: Benchmark-First Toolkit for Ambient RNA Decontamination Research
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("Kushal Raj", "Roy", email = "kushalrajroy1@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4664-7462"))
Description: A research toolkit for developing and honestly evaluating ambient
    RNA decontamination methods for single-cell and single-nucleus RNA-seq.
    Ships a ground-truth simulator with stress settings, a calibrated
    cluster-pooled contamination-fraction estimator, sparse-matrix-safe
    mass-conserving correction that cannot fabricate counts, splice-aware
    layer correction for RNA velocity, hierarchical multi-sample soup pooling,
    genotype-aware contamination estimation, and a metric suite mirroring the
    published benchmarks. Every component is enabled by default only after it
    passes a falsification gate against ground truth. NOTE: name "Decant" is a
    working placeholder and must be checked against CRAN/Bioconductor/GitHub
    before any release.
